WEBVTT

00:33.701 --> 00:37.080
In the far distant future,

00:38.831 --> 00:42.835
when cars are giving up their wheels in the changeover to air-cars,

00:44.504 --> 00:48.299
there still exist fools...

00:49.884 --> 00:53.346
who carry on a vanishing spirit of racing...

00:53.346 --> 00:54.055
who carry on a vanishing spirit oi racing... And
the lead pack has entered the long, long pass.

00:54.055 --> 00:57.267
And the lead pack
has entered the long, long pass.

00:57.433 --> 01:00.937
In the meantime,
the relay units have begun...

01:00.937 --> 01:03.356
...moving on to the water stop here.

01:03.982 --> 01:06.276
Even after two interplanetary wars,

01:06.276 --> 01:09.362
REDLINE's still as popular
as ever with the public.

01:10.113 --> 01:14.242
This is the true ultimate race,
where anything goes.

01:14.242 --> 01:15.618
My money's on Sonoshee.

01:15.618 --> 01:18.997
You really like her, huh?
I put mine on Deguon.

01:19.664 --> 01:20.582
The only rule is that racers must use retro-style engines...
You're kidding!

01:20.582 --> 01:21.291
The only rule is that racers must use retro-style engines...
So'?

01:21.291 --> 01:22.083
The only rule is that racers must use retro-style engines...
I can't.

01:22.083 --> 01:23.251
The only rule is that racers must use retro-style engines...
You stink!

01:23.251 --> 01:25.169
Instead of the currently mainstream anti-gravity engine.
You can squeeze 'm!

01:25.169 --> 01:25.878
Instead of the currently mainstream anti-gravity engine.

01:26.921 --> 01:29.090
Once again, 2358 teams have entered from all over...

01:29.090 --> 01:30.383
Once again, 2358 teams have entered from all over...
Who did you bet on'?

01:30.383 --> 01:31.384
In pursuit of the title "The Fastest in Space.“
JP.

01:31.384 --> 01:32.635
In pursuit of the title "The Fastest in Space."
No way'.!

01:32.635 --> 01:33.595
In pursuit of the title "The Fastest in Space. ”

01:33.595 --> 01:34.137
in pursuit of the title "The Fastest in Space."
Papa'. Where were you'?

01:34.137 --> 01:34.679
Papa! Where were you?

01:34.679 --> 01:35.096
149 teams qualified in the BLUELINE preliminary races
from their home worlds, Papa'. Where were you'?

01:35.096 --> 01:38.266
149 teams qualified in the BLUELINE
preliminary races from their home worlds,

01:38.266 --> 01:40.977
while 6 teams made it through the YELLOWLINE race.

01:40.977 --> 01:43.396
while 6 teams made it through the YELLOWLINE race.
Papa! This way! Hurry!

01:43.396 --> 01:44.981
A battle for the last spot is now raging here at YELLOWLINE.
Papa! This way! Hurry!

01:44.981 --> 01:48.443
The venue for REDLINE is still under wraps.

01:48.443 --> 01:51.321
We're all curious to see the result of viewers' request.

01:51.321 --> 01:54.490
Once the winner of YELLOWLINE is determined,

01:54.490 --> 01:56.075
REDLINE's venue will be announced.

01:56.075 --> 01:57.452
Get around to the right.

01:57.452 --> 01:58.328
Okay-

01:58.328 --> 02:01.664
Our own relay unit Portal has
just arrived at the final relay point.

02:01.664 --> 02:04.834
Papa! A Portal is here!

02:04.834 --> 02:06.669
It's a Portal! Look!

02:06.669 --> 02:10.715
Now, let's get back to the race
and see who's coming first.

02:11.966 --> 02:13.426
Don't push me!

02:25.813 --> 02:28.399
Papa! Get the camera, quick!

02:30.109 --> 02:33.279
It's upside down, Papa!

02:37.241 --> 02:40.787
Papa! The lens cap's on!

02:52.965 --> 02:57.512
Wow! Did you see that?! So cool!

03:09.732 --> 03:13.861
Only 50 klicks left in the Planet Dorothy YELLOWLINE.

03:13.861 --> 03:16.239
Against everyone's expectations,

03:16.239 --> 03:20.410
Cherry Boy Hunter Sonoshee McLaren's
hover jet is still the lead,

03:20.410 --> 03:24.038
She's heading straight toward
the goal in Crab Sonoshee.

03:25.039 --> 03:28.418
And there's the very first
REDLINE champion:

03:28.418 --> 03:31.713
Captain-2-Block's
Captain the Classic in second.

03:31.713 --> 03:34.090
Followed by the REDLINE regular,

03:34.090 --> 03:37.301
Count Markdie and Spark in their Snake Head.

03:37.301 --> 03:39.345
Coming up fourth is Lynchman's archenemy,

03:39.345 --> 03:42.640
Psychoman & Lotten's Psycho Rod.

03:42.640 --> 03:44.600
With these 4 leading the race,

03:44.600 --> 03:48.438
the second group is coming up
14 seconds behind them.

03:48.438 --> 03:50.940
From Planet Supergrass,

03:50.940 --> 03:53.651
ruled by the Princess with magical powers,

03:53.651 --> 03:55.778
Deguon's Fire Bird is leading the group.

03:55.778 --> 04:00.158
Right behind her is Planet Dorothy's
own Bans Missile-EP4.

04:00.158 --> 04:04.912
And bringing up the rear is
Sweet JP's Trans-Am.

04:04.912 --> 04:07.915
The other racers are left way behind.

04:07.915 --> 04:11.502
Looks like it's down to these seven.

04:11.502 --> 04:16.048
Though I have my doubts about JP at this stage.

04:16.048 --> 04:17.216
Oh, you got doubts?

04:17.967 --> 04:22.138
Just trying to make things interesting here.

04:23.222 --> 04:25.183
What do you announcers...

04:25.183 --> 04:27.268
...know about racing?

04:45.286 --> 04:48.581
JP's uncorked the nitro on the final stretch!

04:48.581 --> 04:50.166
He's making a break for it!

04:50.166 --> 04:53.377
He's broken away from the
second group on a rocket ride!

04:54.170 --> 04:57.715
Crab Sonoshee is hanging on to the lead.

04:57.924 --> 05:02.220
Look out!
JP's Trans-Am is on its tail!

05:19.862 --> 05:21.322
Take this!

05:29.622 --> 05:32.124
Look at those
fantastic moves from JP!

05:33.918 --> 05:35.545
This has turned into one hell of a battle!

05:35.545 --> 05:37.630
The crowds must be going wild.

05:39.632 --> 05:43.261
Captain the Classic moves up on Crab Sonoshee.

05:56.399 --> 05:57.066
Punk!

06:14.333 --> 06:19.213
He held back till the last quarter, like you said.

06:19.213 --> 06:23.634
He's the odds on favorite near the finish.

06:24.010 --> 06:28.139
Everything's hunky dory, huh Frisbee?

06:28.139 --> 06:33.352
If there's anyone who can
pull off a fix like this, it's JP.

06:33.352 --> 06:36.147
None of these guys can beat him
at the YELLOWLINE.

06:36.522 --> 06:38.316
That's what you say.

06:39.734 --> 06:44.530
You don't think JP would
try to win this, do you?

06:44.739 --> 06:46.032
Not a chance.

06:46.240 --> 06:50.828
But if he wins, he qualifies for REDLINE.

06:50.828 --> 06:55.374
You don't think he may just decide to go for it?

06:55.708 --> 06:59.003
That won't happen. I can guarantee that.

07:17.939 --> 07:20.358
You're becoming a nuisance,
Cherry Boy Hunter!

07:33.913 --> 07:38.751
Crab Sonoshee hover jet takes a chance
by diving into the river:

07:39.168 --> 07:40.503
You're not getting away!

08:06.779 --> 08:09.281
I'll send you all to hell!

08:44.859 --> 08:45.651
Here we go!

09:07.590 --> 09:12.094
You know Frisbee, if JP wins,

09:12.094 --> 09:16.932
the syndicate's gonna take a big hit.

09:16.932 --> 09:20.895
Look, he isn't called Sweet JP for nothing.

09:20.895 --> 09:24.565
Besides, he wouldn't risk going back in the joint.

09:27.735 --> 09:33.866
Sweet JP, huh? I hope you're right.

09:34.075 --> 09:36.077
Bids are locked.

09:36.077 --> 09:37.536
And our position on JP?

09:37.536 --> 09:39.747
All unloaded.

09:39.747 --> 09:40.915
Good.

09:40.915 --> 09:47.630
Now we'll see how your friendship with JP plays out.

10:04.563 --> 10:05.648
Hold it, hold it...

10:05.898 --> 10:06.607
Now!!

10:40.850 --> 10:46.647
Overtaking Crab Sonoshee,
JP finally takes the lead!

10:46.647 --> 10:48.649
Nobody can catch him now.

10:48.649 --> 10:52.069
He's charging straight for
the finish line on nitro boost!

11:58.427 --> 11:58.802
YES!

13:11.333 --> 13:14.878
You guys aren't just amateurs.
You're total shit!

13:14.878 --> 13:16.505
Shit racers!

13:19.717 --> 13:21.343
Let's go.

14:06.388 --> 14:07.931
Thank you!

14:08.766 --> 14:13.437
Sonoshee McLaren won the
Planet Dorothy YELLOWLINE.

14:13.437 --> 14:15.522
A new queen of racing is born!

14:15.522 --> 14:18.525
And the ticket to REDLINE is hers.

14:18.525 --> 14:20.652
Listen to the crowd!

14:20.652 --> 14:24.782
This completes the lineup of racers for REDLINE.

14:25.199 --> 14:28.410
And the venue for the big race
will be announced shortly.

15:08.409 --> 15:09.243
Look.

15:12.913 --> 15:14.248
What? You first.

15:14.623 --> 15:15.749
No, you go.-

15:16.208 --> 15:17.751
Look, just go first.

15:18.168 --> 15:19.753
You go first.

15:19.962 --> 15:21.755
You go first.

15:26.802 --> 15:29.263
That Trans-Am must cost a fortune.

15:32.099 --> 15:35.269
You couldn't possibly put together a machine like that.

15:41.859 --> 15:44.319
You knew exactly what you were getting into.

15:44.319 --> 15:46.488
You're off the hook with your bondsman now.

15:47.823 --> 15:49.867
That should cover your hospital bill and more.

15:49.867 --> 15:52.035
I'd say it's a win-win.

15:53.704 --> 15:56.707
Racers and mechanics gotta stick together.

15:56.707 --> 15:58.709
You and I have
always made a good team.

16:01.003 --> 16:03.797
Call me when you
wanna get back in the game.

16:04.756 --> 16:06.967
We can make tons of money
as a team, you know.

16:10.637 --> 16:12.973
What the fuck was that for?!

16:14.433 --> 16:17.311
I changed my mind.
It's all yours.

16:17.311 --> 16:19.897
What's this?
An attack of principles?

16:19.897 --> 16:21.148
What about your bondsman?!

16:21.356 --> 16:24.151
So I go back in.
Probably better off.

16:26.111 --> 16:27.905
Whoa! What the hell?!

16:27.905 --> 16:29.615
Hold it! Hold it!

16:30.324 --> 16:33.327
JP! How do you feel about
going to REDLINE?

16:33.327 --> 16:36.538
Sweet JP! How about
a big smile for our camera?

16:36.538 --> 16:39.082
Hey! Leave me out of this!
No pictures!

16:39.082 --> 16:42.961
Are you really going for the race?
Will you drop out?

16:42.961 --> 16:47.799
What are you talking about?
I just blew the YELLOWLINE.

16:47.799 --> 16:48.675
Right.

16:48.675 --> 16:50.093
You mean you don't know?

16:50.302 --> 16:51.094
Huh?

16:52.304 --> 16:54.181
To replace the already declined...

16:54.181 --> 16:56.808
KURUKURU=DAZA
and SHOTO=O-JIN,

16:56.808 --> 17:00.270
the team Miki & Todoroki,
the winner of the Blue Line,

17:00.270 --> 17:05.692
and JP who made a brilliant run at the
YELLOWLINE, have been nominated.

17:05.692 --> 17:06.109
Seriously?

17:06.485 --> 17:07.110
What?

17:07.402 --> 17:09.947
They just announced
the next REDLINE's venue.

17:09.947 --> 17:11.907
It'll be at Roboworld. Roboworld!

17:11.907 --> 17:13.575
Roboworld?!

17:13.575 --> 17:16.161
Roboworld?

17:16.161 --> 17:19.873
My beloved people
of the M3 nebula!

17:19.873 --> 17:24.211
I will not allow the REDLINE
to enter our Roboworld!

17:24.211 --> 17:29.633
Shame on those REDLINE criminals
for disturbing the peace of our nebula!

17:29.633 --> 17:34.805
Our Roboworld exists as
a symbol of peace for humanity.

17:34.805 --> 17:38.517
I can never allow REDLINE
to enter this sacred place!

17:38.934 --> 17:41.395
Any REDLINE outsiders
who invade our territory...

17:41.395 --> 17:43.772
will be destroyed,
by any means necessary!

17:43.772 --> 17:45.440
Come on, there's no way.

17:45.440 --> 17:47.568
They just announced
a few minutes ago...

17:47.568 --> 17:50.487
that the next REDLINE's
gonna be held at Roboworld.

17:50.487 --> 17:52.614
I can't believe they're allowing this.

17:52.614 --> 17:54.533
That's just it. They're not.

17:54.908 --> 17:55.576
Thought so.

17:55.576 --> 18:00.706
That's why KURUKURU=DAZA
and SHOTO=O-JIN dropped out.

18:00.706 --> 18:03.709
I was gonna be in it for fun, you know?

18:03.709 --> 18:08.463
There's no way I'm gonna race
while I get attacked by some army!

18:08.463 --> 18:10.465
Good point.

18:10.465 --> 18:14.636
I'm a racer now, not a soldier:
I've had enough of that shit.

18:15.721 --> 18:17.723
I can't do it.

18:17.723 --> 18:20.976
Roboworld is an important client
of my kingdom.

18:20.976 --> 18:23.478
I'm not ready to give up
my life just yet.

18:24.855 --> 18:29.484
So after the popularity poll,
the top 2 teams were picked.

18:33.989 --> 18:35.490
I see...

18:37.367 --> 18:40.871
JP, are you going?

18:40.871 --> 18:42.789
Or will you drop out?

18:42.789 --> 18:44.541
JP, please make a statement!

18:44.541 --> 18:46.668
I take it back, Frisbee.

18:47.044 --> 18:49.004
Fix up the Trans-Am, will you?

18:49.004 --> 18:49.588
What?

18:49.588 --> 18:51.840
So you're going, then?

18:51.840 --> 18:54.551
Is that official, JP?
He won't.

18:54.551 --> 18:57.054
Please give us a comment, JP! A simple yes or no!
Think twice before you say something.

18:57.054 --> 18:58.555
Please give us a comment, JP! A simple yes or no!

18:58.555 --> 19:00.474
Give me the camera.

19:02.225 --> 19:04.936
Watch out, Roboworld! Here comes JP!

19:06.605 --> 19:11.360
All right! He's in! JP's in! And there you
have it from JP who has qualified for REDLINE.

19:11.568 --> 19:15.322
Oh goody! It's time for the festival of fools again!

19:15.322 --> 19:17.366
I like rough sports every now and then.

19:25.791 --> 19:27.876
PAROLE

19:28.293 --> 19:28.502
SATELLITE EUROPASS

19:28.502 --> 19:33.006
SATELLITE EUROPASS
The ship is approaching Roboworld's satellite, Europass.

19:33.006 --> 19:33.590
The ship is approaching Roboworld's satellite, Europass.

19:34.299 --> 19:38.178
Please prepare for landing in your designated pod.

19:40.138 --> 19:44.142
The ship is approaching Roboworld's satellite, Europass.

19:44.351 --> 19:46.770
Please prepare for landing in your designated pod.

19:57.406 --> 20:00.200
Wow! It's picking up speed.

20:00.200 --> 20:03.286
Flaps... Flaps...
Where's the flaps button?

20:08.917 --> 20:11.002
Is this a coffin or what?!

20:11.002 --> 20:16.425
This is nothing but a serious act
of aggression against Roboworld!

20:17.217 --> 20:19.094
Secretary Titan!

20:19.094 --> 20:19.553
Si"

20:19.553 --> 20:22.222
You must have something to report!

20:22.222 --> 20:24.850
I just received a message from our scout vessels.

20:24.850 --> 20:30.147
They identified a group of ships on Europass's surface.

20:30.439 --> 20:31.940
Europass?

20:31.940 --> 20:32.649
Yes.

20:32.649 --> 20:36.611
The planet we donated to those pathetic refugees.

20:36.611 --> 20:43.869
It's demilitarized under our treaty
with the M3 Nebula Federation.

20:43.869 --> 20:45.912
That means our forces must tread very carefully there.

20:46.163 --> 20:50.584
Besides, the refugees from
nearby sectors have drifted in...

20:50.584 --> 20:53.170
and set up slums all over the place.

20:53.378 --> 20:57.299
It's an ideal hideout for REDLINE racers.

20:58.008 --> 21:00.719
This is what we get
for being so generous!

21:03.013 --> 21:07.267
They have the audacity to claim it's
by the viewers' request.

21:07.267 --> 21:12.522
Don't they know we can't put
our military secrets at risk?

21:12.522 --> 21:16.443
There's no way we'd allow
a stupid race in such a sacred place!

21:16.443 --> 21:18.737
Mr. President.

21:23.700 --> 21:25.243
Are you all right, sir?

21:26.953 --> 21:28.622
Mr. President!

21:28.622 --> 21:29.414
What?

21:29.414 --> 21:32.626
You're not going to stand by and let them pass, are you?

21:32.626 --> 21:34.836
I make the rules on this planet!

21:34.836 --> 21:39.549
All those affiliated with REDLINE are
guilty and deserve to be hanged!

21:39.549 --> 21:41.676
As president, I'll take full responsibility!

21:41.676 --> 21:44.805
Because I represent justice.

21:44.805 --> 21:47.933
The entire universe is in need of strong leadership,

21:47.933 --> 21:54.272
and Roboworld stands
heroically by its principals!

21:55.357 --> 21:57.859
Colonel Volton!

21:57.859 --> 21:58.777
Si"

21:58.777 --> 22:01.446
Are you ready to shed your blood for justice?

22:01.446 --> 22:03.240
Sir! More than ready, sir!

22:03.240 --> 22:07.661
Good! Fight with your life for ultimate justice!

22:08.703 --> 22:10.330
Thank you, sir!

22:17.838 --> 22:18.672
Hey, you!

22:19.923 --> 22:20.966
Hey, I'm talking to you!

22:20.966 --> 22:24.302
Don't you ignore me!
Buy a ticket for REDLINE, will ya?

22:25.011 --> 22:26.096
Don't ignore me!

22:26.096 --> 22:28.473
You have money, don't you?

22:30.267 --> 22:33.061
How about I give you a discount?

22:33.770 --> 22:35.939
What happened there?

22:37.190 --> 22:38.733
Get off me.

22:38.733 --> 22:40.193
What happened?

22:40.193 --> 22:43.405
Stop it! Sorry to disappoint,
but I'm not here to watch.

22:44.573 --> 22:46.408
Useless! You're so totally useless to us!

22:46.408 --> 22:47.951
Ahh...fuck!

22:48.743 --> 22:49.619
Wait!

22:50.579 --> 22:54.457
1, 2, s, 4...

22:58.545 --> 22:59.379
Next!

23:00.881 --> 23:02.257
What is this?

23:02.257 --> 23:04.676
You're sure about the exchange rate?

23:04.676 --> 23:06.177
Just about right. Next!

23:06.970 --> 23:09.598
Just about? What the heck is that?

23:09.598 --> 23:11.433
You need to take money more serious...

23:11.433 --> 23:12.475
You're annoying!

23:22.611 --> 23:23.528
Right here.

23:24.863 --> 23:25.906
What?

23:25.906 --> 23:27.282
Need some smokes.

23:27.282 --> 23:27.866
Got money?

23:28.783 --> 23:32.078
Sure. I just cashed in.

23:32.078 --> 23:35.165
Give me as many as this will get.

23:40.712 --> 23:41.588
Here.

23:42.756 --> 23:44.633
What, is this it?

23:44.633 --> 23:46.009
It's already open.

23:47.302 --> 23:49.512
This ain't right.

23:49.512 --> 23:51.848
Hey, Grandma!
Money needs to be taken...

23:52.098 --> 23:54.726
Don't like it? Then leave it.

23:54.726 --> 23:57.562
Just leave it and walk away!

24:04.194 --> 24:04.778
Huh?

24:12.452 --> 24:13.536
Whoops.

24:17.666 --> 24:19.209
Whoa! Whoa!

24:21.962 --> 24:24.297
View's clear!

24:25.131 --> 24:28.259
Good. Let's roll!

24:34.641 --> 24:35.600
Nice!

24:35.892 --> 24:37.769
These antigravity engines aren't bad!

24:38.561 --> 24:41.147
Yeah, not bad at all!

25:01.793 --> 25:02.627
Done.

25:07.257 --> 25:09.217
Oh, it's you, JP.

25:09.217 --> 25:11.386
This planet is really something, huh?

25:11.386 --> 25:12.762
What did you expect?

25:12.762 --> 25:16.349
This place gets flotsam from all over the galaxy.

25:16.349 --> 25:20.020
It's hard for the idea of service to sink in.

25:20.020 --> 25:21.604
How are you holding up?

25:23.898 --> 25:25.442
Alright, I guess... Ouch!

25:26.109 --> 25:27.902
Yeah, I can see that.

25:32.365 --> 25:33.491
Ow... Ow...

25:36.244 --> 25:40.331
I got an attaché case from Frisbee.
It was stuffed with cash.

25:40.331 --> 25:42.250
Yeah, it's for fixing up
the Trans-Am.

25:42.250 --> 25:46.755
He used to drop everything
to work on your machine.

25:47.005 --> 25:49.507
He sure has changed.

25:49.507 --> 25:51.843
Like you, me, and everything else.

25:51.843 --> 25:55.513
Cigs cost more and good junk joints
are harder to find.

26:02.187 --> 26:04.272
So, where's my Trans-Am?

26:15.283 --> 26:18.453
You really did it this time,
you ingrate.

26:18.453 --> 26:21.956
What were you thinking,
using the nitro twice?

26:21.956 --> 26:24.626
You got a death wish?

26:25.335 --> 26:27.504
I'll need three caps for the REDLINE.

26:28.546 --> 26:29.464
Three?!

26:29.798 --> 26:31.716
Hey, watch it, Pops!

26:32.133 --> 26:34.594
This is a totally different level
than the YELLOWLINE.

26:34.594 --> 26:37.680
I'm gonna need an edge, won't I?

26:37.847 --> 26:40.350
Then get your machine armed up.

26:40.350 --> 26:44.604
You know that
anything goes at REDLINE.

26:44.604 --> 26:46.606
I can get you armed up good.

26:46.606 --> 26:49.484
REDLINE's a race, not a war.

26:49.484 --> 26:51.236
Keep that crap off of my machine.

26:51.236 --> 26:54.948
I see you're as stupidly soft
as your nickname implies.

26:54.948 --> 26:56.699
Don't call me that!

26:56.699 --> 27:00.912
In the REDLINE, you can attack or
interfere with the others any way you want.

27:00.912 --> 27:05.458
You're behind the times
by trying to play fair.

27:05.458 --> 27:07.627
Behind the times, huh?

27:08.837 --> 27:15.093
30 years in this business and
I still got my chops. Not bad, huh?

27:15.093 --> 27:19.806
I clean up good with all
the trades I get at the race.

27:19.806 --> 27:23.893
A little fun on the side wouldn't hurt, either.

27:23.893 --> 27:26.187
A little fun.

27:27.147 --> 27:28.523
Listen, JP.

27:29.607 --> 27:32.819
If you want a stove that'll stand up to 3 caps of juice,

27:32.819 --> 27:35.029
you're talking a redesign from scratch.

27:35.029 --> 27:36.906
If you don't want to use weapons,

27:36.906 --> 27:40.660
all I can do is to get you
a new engine and custom parts.

27:40.660 --> 27:43.329
I wish I could do more.

27:43.329 --> 27:45.665
Hey, you listening to me?

27:46.291 --> 27:48.251
Frisbee can handle
the redesigning and tune-up.

27:48.501 --> 27:49.711
You're joking.

27:49.711 --> 27:50.628
Huh? Why?

27:52.589 --> 27:55.049
When was the last time
you two worked as a team?

27:55.049 --> 27:55.758
Stop it.

27:55.758 --> 27:57.760
Frisbee's not legit anymore.

27:57.760 --> 27:59.762
Cut it out!
He's sold out. He's no good!

27:59.762 --> 28:00.680
He's sold out. He's no good!

28:07.520 --> 28:08.521
Talking about the fix?

28:09.480 --> 28:13.067
He's not the same man. You know that, right?

28:13.067 --> 28:16.321
Helping an ingrate like you is no big deal,

28:16.321 --> 28:19.449
but getting mixed up with that scum is another story.

28:19.449 --> 28:22.035
Racers and mechanics
gotta stick together.

28:22.744 --> 28:26.289
You and I make a good team.
Always have.

28:27.123 --> 28:28.791
Hey, Frisbee.
Took you long enough.

28:29.209 --> 28:33.630
I may be a scum,
but I still got the touch, you know.

28:33.630 --> 28:35.798
Don't judge a man's skill by his character.

28:36.716 --> 28:40.553
So, you've also learned to
sneak around now, Frisbee?

28:43.014 --> 28:44.432
Relax, Pops.

28:44.432 --> 28:47.727
If I didn't have the touch,
I wouldn't still be here.

28:48.561 --> 28:51.231
Nobody's worried about your touch.

28:53.650 --> 28:55.026
The old man's on board.

28:55.026 --> 28:57.153
I didn't agree to anything.

28:57.153 --> 28:59.405
Hey, quit that!

28:59.405 --> 29:01.324
I guess I'll leave it to the two of you now.

29:01.324 --> 29:02.867
Hey! Where are you going?

29:05.620 --> 29:08.122
The old man will get a new engine.

29:08.122 --> 29:11.292
Frisbee'll take care of the redesign and mods.

29:11.292 --> 29:14.671
I'll do my job when I put my butt behind the wheel.

29:15.505 --> 29:17.674
Until then, I'll leave everything to you pros.

29:18.508 --> 29:20.301
Like the old days.

29:21.844 --> 29:23.846
He think he's cool or something?

29:40.905 --> 29:42.031
What do you want?

29:43.825 --> 29:46.035
This ain't your seat, punk!

29:46.035 --> 29:47.537
You want some?!

29:48.788 --> 29:52.875
Oh, a comb...
Don't scare me, you fool!

29:52.875 --> 29:56.045
I see you're having a full house today, waiter.

29:56.045 --> 29:57.672
I'm the manager, you jerk!

29:57.672 --> 29:59.841
And enough with the wisecracks!
The place is deserted.

29:59.841 --> 30:02.885
Just pick a table and settle down, will ya?

30:02.885 --> 30:03.678
Okay, okay.

30:04.387 --> 30:06.472
Sorry about that, Miss.

30:07.557 --> 30:11.477
He won't bother you anymore,
so don't worry.

30:12.228 --> 30:15.606
Here's your soup spaghetti
a la Europass lobster.

30:15.606 --> 30:17.025
Looks great!

30:17.025 --> 30:18.693
Enjoy your meal.

30:18.693 --> 30:19.902
Thank you.

30:28.661 --> 30:31.080
You're breaking the dress code, Manager.

30:31.080 --> 30:33.082
Oh, no! How embarrassing!

30:33.082 --> 30:34.250
What are you doing?

30:34.250 --> 30:35.209
Nothing.

30:35.209 --> 30:36.794
No, seriously.

30:37.754 --> 30:40.298
Excuse me. I'm JP.

30:40.298 --> 30:41.591
JP?

30:41.591 --> 30:42.967
Are you gonna eat that?

30:42.967 --> 30:43.676
Huh?

30:44.969 --> 30:45.553
What's this?

30:50.975 --> 30:51.934
Give me a break...

30:52.602 --> 30:54.937
Mind if I join you?

30:55.271 --> 30:57.440
Sorry, I'm waiting for someone.

30:58.358 --> 30:59.067
Bummer.

31:00.109 --> 31:05.198
I remember now!
You're that guy from the YELLOWLINE.

31:05.198 --> 31:07.867
You're going to REDLINE
as a substitute, right?

31:07.867 --> 31:08.451
What do you want?

31:10.161 --> 31:14.207
I thought I'd check you out
since you're going, too.

31:14.207 --> 31:14.916
Come again?

31:17.168 --> 31:18.378
She saw my underpants...

31:18.378 --> 31:21.839
Winning the YELLOWLINE with a hover engine...

31:21.839 --> 31:25.093
was so cool that I wanted to
check out the racer for myself.

31:25.093 --> 31:26.386
And the verdict?

31:27.470 --> 31:30.139
Verdict? Well...

31:30.139 --> 31:34.519
I see an engine geek with no interest in men.

31:34.519 --> 31:35.436
Bingo.

31:35.436 --> 31:39.941
Wheels are my only love.
I've known nothing but racing since I was a kid.

31:40.149 --> 31:43.945
So, you're one of those sad types who
can't make any human friends, huh?

31:44.779 --> 31:47.031
Meaning what?
Why don't you just go now?

31:52.870 --> 31:54.664
My dad was a racer.

31:55.790 --> 31:57.250
We owned a junk joint.

31:57.250 --> 31:59.961
We used to build our own
machines to enter races.

32:00.711 --> 32:01.587
I see.

32:03.423 --> 32:07.218
It was the most natural thing to do...

32:07.218 --> 32:08.136
What's that?

32:09.470 --> 32:12.723
Steamlight. Isn't it pretty?

32:13.558 --> 32:16.727
My Dad gave it to me on my 7th birthday.

32:18.896 --> 32:22.358
So this is a steamlight, huh?
I've never seen one before.

32:22.358 --> 32:25.153
They say when burned as fuel,

32:25.153 --> 32:28.573
it releases 100 times more energy
than gold nitro.

32:28.573 --> 32:29.991
No kidding.

32:30.199 --> 32:33.244
This is my first time seeing real steamlight, too.

32:33.953 --> 32:36.164
An energy source with unlimited capacity.

32:37.165 --> 32:42.003
No man can handle that
amount of power, though.

32:42.003 --> 32:43.546
You know a lot, don't you?

32:43.546 --> 32:46.799
Oh, how do you do.
I'm Shinkai.

32:46.799 --> 32:48.384
Pleased to meet you.

32:48.384 --> 32:51.846
Aren't you gonna eat that?
Hexagonal worm spaghetti soup.

32:51.846 --> 32:52.972
It's so good!

32:53.806 --> 32:55.266
Please have some.

32:55.266 --> 32:56.058
Hooray!

32:57.351 --> 32:59.979
May I perhaps taste some of you as well tonight?

33:03.357 --> 33:04.484
Yummy time!

33:05.443 --> 33:08.529
She would have been mine
if you hadn't interrupted.

33:08.529 --> 33:10.364
Mr. Substitute.

33:11.199 --> 33:12.783
Call me a reserve.

33:13.910 --> 33:17.705
You guys are racers, right?
I saw you on the news.

33:17.705 --> 33:19.749
I'm a racer myself, you know.

33:19.749 --> 33:23.377
Though I must say I'm more known as a mechanic.

33:23.377 --> 33:27.006
I have a partner named Trava.

33:27.006 --> 33:28.007
Trava?

33:29.967 --> 33:31.177
Let me go!

33:33.679 --> 33:36.349
Stop trashing the place! Take it outside!

33:37.141 --> 33:38.476
Trava!

33:38.476 --> 33:39.519
Your partner?

33:39.519 --> 33:41.604
The one getting beaten up, yes.

33:41.604 --> 33:42.730
Which one is that?

33:44.482 --> 33:46.817
Hey, that hurt!

33:46.817 --> 33:48.528
You started it.

33:48.861 --> 33:51.030
Shit! Here he goes!

33:51.280 --> 33:53.449
It's your fault, damn it!

33:53.449 --> 33:55.660
You betrayed the army.

33:55.660 --> 33:58.162
Is the tough guy crying?

33:58.162 --> 33:59.997
That's Little Deyzuna.

33:59.997 --> 34:03.543
He used to be in the army with us.

34:03.543 --> 34:06.087
He becomes impossibly strong when he cries.

34:15.555 --> 34:18.057
Having a race on Roboworld!

34:18.057 --> 34:20.977
You're just doing that to make me suffer!

34:22.478 --> 34:23.938
That's bullshit!

34:23.938 --> 34:26.065
It's nothing personal and you know it!

34:26.065 --> 34:27.608
Liar!

34:43.291 --> 34:45.710
Hm. More weirdoes on the scene.

34:50.172 --> 34:54.093
Well, if it ain't Machine Head Tetsuzin himself.

34:54.093 --> 34:55.886
That's really Machine Head?

34:57.388 --> 34:59.724
Mr. REDLINE.
The fastest man in the galaxy.

35:04.395 --> 35:05.479
Outta my way.

35:06.397 --> 35:07.982
Don't order me around!

35:08.232 --> 35:10.568
I said, outta my way!

35:10.568 --> 35:13.487
You think you can order me around?

35:13.779 --> 35:15.781
I'm just telling you to move.

35:15.781 --> 35:17.700
That's an order, you moron!

35:17.700 --> 35:21.245
Fine, if you won't move,
I'll go around you.

35:25.416 --> 35:29.086
That's what you get
when you mess with me!

35:29.086 --> 35:31.005
To hell with the race!

35:48.439 --> 35:49.607
Sonoshee!

35:52.151 --> 35:53.277
This way!

36:17.968 --> 36:18.928
What?

36:18.928 --> 36:20.471
Looks like Roboworld forces.

36:33.567 --> 36:36.487
You're a hard man to find,
Little Deyzuna.

36:38.030 --> 36:40.032
Colonel Volton!

36:40.032 --> 36:43.119
You weren't ordered
to leave the base.

36:43.536 --> 36:46.706
I told you to stay put, didn't I?

36:46.706 --> 36:48.666
Look what you did!

36:55.172 --> 36:57.174
Thanks for coming here personally...

36:57.174 --> 37:00.469
to deal with your insubordinate
subordinate, Col. Volton.

37:01.220 --> 37:02.263
Stay there!

37:03.889 --> 37:08.561
This is a demilitarized zone.
We won't stand for this.

37:08.561 --> 37:10.438
So what?

37:10.438 --> 37:12.106
I said so what?

37:12.106 --> 37:16.235
Are Roboworld soldiers
hard of hearing?

37:18.320 --> 37:24.160
Oh, I can hear you fine.
I just don't need your permission.

37:24.160 --> 37:26.704
Doesn't matter. I got what I came for.

37:26.704 --> 37:31.208
Oh, yes, and I have orders to
use force on the day of the race.

37:31.208 --> 37:32.376
Seriously?!

37:32.376 --> 37:34.879
Volton's Hell Troops have been
ordered into action?

37:43.304 --> 37:49.185
The president generously offered
his presence at your silly race.

37:49.185 --> 37:54.148
You should try to be good targets
for our troops in return.

37:54.148 --> 37:57.276
I suppose having your heads can wait.

37:57.276 --> 37:57.902
Hey, you!

37:58.694 --> 38:01.530
Don't try something stupid.

38:07.578 --> 38:11.832
The air in here's kinda stuffy
since you guys walked in.

38:12.708 --> 38:13.709
Beat it.

38:15.419 --> 38:19.215
You've got seven guns
pointed at you.

38:20.549 --> 38:22.176
Nice. That'll solve my...

38:27.681 --> 38:28.474
Ow.

38:42.071 --> 38:43.155
Ow!

38:43.155 --> 38:44.907
That hurts...

38:44.907 --> 38:46.116
How's your head?

38:46.992 --> 38:48.536
I'll live.

38:49.620 --> 38:51.080
What were you thinking?

38:51.080 --> 38:55.751
Those bastards were really trying my patience.

38:56.126 --> 38:57.294
Couldn't help it.

38:58.087 --> 39:01.257
You got your plans all
screwed up by them, too.

39:01.674 --> 39:03.300
I guess you're right.

39:03.300 --> 39:08.472
Thanks for this.
You really are sweet, aren't you?

39:08.472 --> 39:10.933
It's a stupid nickname for the fans,

39:10.933 --> 39:13.853
Cherry Boy Hunter Sonoshee McLaren.

39:13.853 --> 39:15.813
Cherry Boy...what's that?

39:15.813 --> 39:17.106
Don't you read the papers?

39:17.106 --> 39:20.442
That nickname of yours made quite a headline.

39:20.442 --> 39:21.819
That's stupid!

39:21.819 --> 39:23.112
Don't look at me.

39:24.154 --> 39:25.406
What was that for?

39:29.618 --> 39:31.161
Why the sour face?

39:31.161 --> 39:32.955
Cherry Boy Hunter...

39:34.081 --> 39:35.416
Can I ask you something?

39:35.791 --> 39:36.792
What?

39:37.668 --> 39:41.130
Why do you race?

39:42.172 --> 39:43.507
Why do you?

39:43.716 --> 39:47.136
Me? Not much to tell.

39:47.136 --> 39:49.013
Then don't ask me.

39:49.972 --> 39:50.973
Sorry.

39:55.269 --> 39:57.897
C'mon! Out with it!

39:57.897 --> 39:59.023
I mean...

39:59.815 --> 40:01.942
it's really no big deal.

40:02.985 --> 40:03.861
Really.

40:11.243 --> 40:12.578
Is that so?

40:16.081 --> 40:19.418
You need more muscles if
you wanna take those bastards.

40:19.668 --> 40:21.587
Good night now.

40:21.587 --> 40:22.421
G'night.

40:33.515 --> 40:35.225
Hey, you dropped this!

40:42.274 --> 40:44.193
Oh, well.

40:44.193 --> 40:45.778
Go faster! Go!

40:46.820 --> 40:48.989
Alright! Go for it!

40:51.367 --> 40:52.826
That was close!

40:52.826 --> 40:54.119
Is she okay?

41:01.502 --> 41:04.838
You did great!
You drive like the wind!

41:04.838 --> 41:07.716
You gave it all you have.
Just forget about it.

41:07.716 --> 41:10.761
I'm gonna race in the REDLINE someday!

41:11.011 --> 41:11.887
What?

41:13.639 --> 41:17.101
I bust my ass off for it everyday.

41:17.101 --> 41:20.270
I can't afford to waste my time like this!

41:21.772 --> 41:25.609
I'm not like you amateurs
who are all talk and no action.

41:28.320 --> 41:32.658
Why don't you quit watching and
get down here with the rest of us?

41:51.260 --> 41:53.053
Wow...

41:59.226 --> 42:01.895
I bet she doesn't remember.

42:08.152 --> 42:09.111
JP!

42:11.697 --> 42:15.993
I'm telling you,
I can't work with this jerk.

42:15.993 --> 42:16.785
Why?

42:16.785 --> 42:19.788
Your pal here says
he doesn't like the engine I got.

42:19.788 --> 42:21.749
You sure about him?

42:21.749 --> 42:23.167
It's REDLINE!

42:23.167 --> 42:27.046
We need something bigger,
or else we're just wasting our time.

42:27.379 --> 42:29.673
We're talking about the race here!

42:29.673 --> 42:31.842
A man is driving!

42:31.842 --> 42:36.138
This guy's talking about
a goddamn TRZ Airmaster, JP!

42:36.138 --> 42:36.930
Seriously?!

42:36.930 --> 42:38.015
Go ahead, laugh!

42:38.015 --> 42:41.393
It's crap!
Powerful, but unstable as hell.

42:41.393 --> 42:43.145
A four cycle TRZ Airmaster!
A four cycle TRZ Airmaster!

42:43.353 --> 42:47.232
All it needs is a dose of
Frisbee magic and it'll be fine.

42:47.232 --> 42:47.983
Like hell!

42:48.942 --> 42:51.320
Besides, JP's driving it.

42:51.320 --> 42:53.989
You think he hasn't got what it takes?

42:53.989 --> 42:57.201
You are the only one I have trouble trusting.

42:58.160 --> 42:59.661
Who do you think you are?

42:59.661 --> 43:00.704
Showing up with all that money,
then you start bossing me around!

43:00.704 --> 43:02.790
Pops! Showing up with all that money,
then you start bossing me around!

43:02.790 --> 43:04.792
Just get him what he wants.

43:04.792 --> 43:06.502
Huh? What was that?

43:06.502 --> 43:07.753
Get him what he needs.

43:07.753 --> 43:09.463
You're gonna get killed!

43:09.463 --> 43:12.841
As far as the design goes,
Frisbee's in charge.

43:12.841 --> 43:14.134
We're a team, right?

43:14.134 --> 43:17.346
Ha! It's all in the past.

43:17.346 --> 43:21.016
You know how long it'll take to get one of those monsters?

43:21.016 --> 43:24.645
It's your job to get what
we need in time for the race.

43:24.645 --> 43:27.397
You're in charge of getting us the engine parts.

43:27.397 --> 43:29.566
Some things just can't be done.

43:29.566 --> 43:31.902
Pops... Please.

43:33.070 --> 43:35.489
Let me race in his machine.

43:35.489 --> 43:40.244
Fine, you fool...
It'll cost you double though.

43:40.244 --> 43:42.079
Thanks, Pops. I owe you one.

43:45.874 --> 43:50.003
TWO DAYS TO REDLINE

43:56.343 --> 43:58.137
Fast, huh?

43:59.596 --> 44:01.765
Not as many racing as I expected.

44:01.765 --> 44:05.978
Guys with money like to
keep it quiet at the private tracks.

44:07.187 --> 44:11.733
Yeah. This is the place for the struggling racers.

44:14.653 --> 44:17.739
Don't worry. Looks like the
engine will make it in time.

44:19.199 --> 44:21.243
He always comes through,
even on impossible jobs like this.

44:22.119 --> 44:23.579
That's our Pops.

44:26.123 --> 44:29.459
I talked to lnuki, by the way.

44:29.459 --> 44:32.713
Same drill as before.

44:32.713 --> 44:36.258
Stay in the rear till the third quarter
to get your odds down.

44:36.633 --> 44:39.428
Then make your move in the last quarter.

44:39.428 --> 44:41.263
Say...

44:41.263 --> 44:45.058
Once I'm in the Trans-Am's seat,
I'm the boss, right?

44:45.058 --> 44:47.895
I'd rather find another way
to pay for the engine.

44:51.148 --> 44:54.234
You may get a spare engine,
but not a spare life.

44:54.234 --> 44:56.403
We really have no choice.

45:02.492 --> 45:04.077
We're all in this together.

45:04.077 --> 45:06.955
Come what sparks or potato chip
crumbs that may fall on us.

45:08.665 --> 45:12.085
ROBOWORLD MINERAL EXTRACTION SITE

45:17.007 --> 45:18.842
That's it for today!

45:18.842 --> 45:21.053
Let's go place our REDLINE bets.

45:21.053 --> 45:21.637
Yeah!

45:22.387 --> 45:23.555
ROBOWORLD ILLEGAL UNDERGROUND BETTING PARLOR

45:23.555 --> 45:24.431
ROBOWORLD ILLEGAL UNDERGROUND BETTING PARLOR
Bet on #4. It's the current favorite to win.

45:24.431 --> 45:27.809
Bet on #4. It's the current favorite to win.

45:28.018 --> 45:29.353
Okay, gimme 100 on #4.

45:29.353 --> 45:30.354
How about you?

45:30.354 --> 45:33.023
I'll take 150 on Gori Rider.

45:33.023 --> 45:35.192
You sure? He always comes in fifth.

45:35.192 --> 45:35.984
It won't hurt.

45:35.984 --> 45:37.361
50 on #2 please.

45:37.361 --> 45:39.238
Don't be stingy. Be bold!

45:39.238 --> 45:40.155
50's fine.

45:40.155 --> 45:41.698
I'll take 300 on JP.

45:42.157 --> 45:44.409
You're betting on a long shot, huh?

45:44.743 --> 45:46.662
The odds'll be 25,000 to 1.

45:47.329 --> 45:48.830
I know.

45:48.830 --> 45:50.290
What the hell?!
What's happening?

45:50.290 --> 45:52.918
Disperse at once!

45:53.669 --> 45:54.586
Shut up!

45:54.586 --> 45:55.337
Give me money!

45:55.504 --> 45:57.839
This is a violation of the law.

46:09.643 --> 46:12.854
Next up is today's segment featuring Crab Sonoshee.

46:13.063 --> 46:19.528
Her new engine can prevent a missile
lock-on by minimizing its heat output.

46:19.528 --> 46:24.199
As you can see on this thermograph chart,
it's much lower than her old engine.

46:24.199 --> 46:26.827
It can now avoid
a missile's heat sensor.

46:26.827 --> 46:28.370
My butt's on camera!

46:30.497 --> 46:35.711
Looks like Crab Sonoshee's engine
mods are going well for REDLINE.

46:36.670 --> 46:38.297
The man of sonic speed.

46:38.297 --> 46:41.091
Since his first win at the fourth REDLINE,

46:41.258 --> 46:46.430
this invincible king's been at the top for 20 years.

46:46.430 --> 46:49.975
The machine integrated racer
who keeps altering himself...

46:49.975 --> 46:52.060
along with his machine “God Wing.”

46:52.311 --> 46:54.688
The irrefutable champion of REDLINE!

46:59.026 --> 47:04.614
King of kings, Mr. REDLINE:
Machine Head Tetsuzin!

47:04.614 --> 47:07.826
Good evening all.
I'm Machine Head Tetsuzin.

47:07.826 --> 47:11.496
Well, for me... How shall I put it?

47:11.496 --> 47:16.543
I'd say I'm in a different league
compared to the others.

47:16.543 --> 47:20.339
'Cause in my case,
I'm a part of my machine.

47:20.339 --> 47:22.799
For the others,
it's "Me and my wheels."

47:22.799 --> 47:25.260
But in my case,
it's "I am my wheels," you see?

47:26.345 --> 47:28.138
He can't underestimate his rivals, though.

47:28.138 --> 47:31.725
The royal family's Boiboi and
Bosbos make their return,

47:31.725 --> 47:36.313
with Princess Supergrass,
the last heir to magical superpowers.

47:36.688 --> 47:39.691
This time around,
they've sealed off their magic.

47:43.862 --> 47:47.074
The carefree beauty pair - Super Boins.

47:47.366 --> 47:52.204
Hi there! I'm the super sexy
and gorgeous racer, Boiboi.

47:52.204 --> 47:57.084
I don't know about that,
but oh well... I'm Bosbos.

47:57.459 --> 48:00.462
We are Super Boins!

48:02.589 --> 48:04.674
Wanna see my specialty?

48:04.674 --> 48:06.885
I can make all kinds of faces.

48:08.637 --> 48:09.346
SEE?

48:12.391 --> 48:14.518
Well? Impressive, huh?

48:14.851 --> 48:17.062
I can make funny faces, too.

48:18.522 --> 48:20.148
So cute!

48:21.358 --> 48:23.693
Now you're creeping me out.

48:23.693 --> 48:25.529
So? What do you say?

48:25.821 --> 48:28.740
Dear Princess!
We are going to win for sure!

48:31.201 --> 48:34.621
Planet Supergrass' racing singing super idol.

48:34.621 --> 48:39.042
Here's their new single, Zooming Gears!

48:43.839 --> 48:45.924
And how can we forget this amazing pair?

48:47.092 --> 48:48.718
Heel hero of Alsatia.

48:48.718 --> 48:50.679
The strongest, fastest bounty hunters!

48:50.679 --> 48:54.266
The Mad Brothers - Lynchman and Johnny Boya!

48:55.851 --> 48:58.979
We're Lynchman and Johnny Boya,
the bounty hunters.

48:58.979 --> 49:00.355
Don't tell me you don't know!

49:00.355 --> 49:02.732
We've never failed catching our targets ever,

49:02.732 --> 49:04.526
'cause we're fast.

49:04.526 --> 49:07.696
That bastard Machine Head
beat us in the last REDLINE,

49:07.696 --> 49:10.323
but with our new machine, it's gonna
be totally different from five years ago!

49:10.490 --> 49:14.703
Wait and see! We'll pay you back
double for last time!

49:14.703 --> 49:15.620
Don't wet your pants, suckers!

49:22.669 --> 49:26.923
Lynchman's best fight #7,
now on sale!

49:30.010 --> 49:31.511
What the hell?

49:31.720 --> 49:35.849
REDLINE EVE

49:37.809 --> 49:39.227
Looking good.

49:39.436 --> 49:41.229
A test car for the image training.

49:41.229 --> 49:44.065
I installed the engine
from an old TRZ Airmaster.

49:44.983 --> 49:46.568
No kidding!

49:46.568 --> 49:48.904
You should be able to get a feel with this.

49:48.904 --> 49:49.946
May I?

49:49.946 --> 49:50.989
Of course.

49:52.949 --> 49:53.950
This is great!

49:54.242 --> 49:55.202
This will do.

50:00.999 --> 50:02.209
Oh! Crab Sonoshee!

50:17.516 --> 50:21.186
Hey, everyone! After his dramatic
crash landing in the YELLOWLINE,

50:21.186 --> 50:23.688
JP's done it again during his latest test run.

50:23.688 --> 50:28.568
After crashing at 300 kph,
he was miraculously uninjured.

50:30.695 --> 50:32.864
A showdown between rivals!

50:34.783 --> 50:38.745
It's the day before the YELLOWLINE
which saw Miki and Todoroki qualify,

50:38.745 --> 50:41.540
and a policeman relentlessly chases speeding cars.

50:44.459 --> 50:48.171
He makes a bull-charge at the BLUELINE champs,

50:48.171 --> 50:50.757
who made it to REDLINE
as reserves.

50:54.928 --> 50:59.057
Dirty Policeman Hamesh Frini,
a.k.a. "Gori Rider"!

50:59.391 --> 51:03.728
The tape shows excessive force
in dealing with a speed violation!

51:03.728 --> 51:07.649
I'll bust them cocky racers
who dare to challenge me...

51:07.649 --> 51:10.485
by any means necessary.
You got that?!

51:10.485 --> 51:13.154
A comment please, Gori Rider.

51:13.154 --> 51:17.909
A police officer, who should be a
moral paragon, engaged in adultery?

51:17.909 --> 51:20.996
Would you care to comment on
your affair with Ms. Yang-Sue?

51:20.996 --> 51:22.622
Shut up!

51:22.622 --> 51:26.918
The vengeful wild pair
from the shining blue planet,

51:26.918 --> 51:29.212
Miki and Todoroki!

51:29.212 --> 51:32.716
With racing charisma that turns
any road into a race course,

51:32.966 --> 51:34.718
they swear to take revenge in the REDLINE.

51:41.516 --> 51:42.851
Gori Rider, you mother fucker!

51:47.856 --> 51:49.566
It's finally here, JP!

51:49.899 --> 51:53.236
Can't get any better than this baby.

51:53.236 --> 51:56.990
That 80 mm thick cylinder block
can give you 35,000 horsepower.

51:56.990 --> 51:58.199
The last Airmaster.

51:58.199 --> 51:59.951
Wow...

51:59.951 --> 52:02.120
It's not a dream.

52:02.120 --> 52:03.788
We finally got it...

52:04.706 --> 52:07.876
Of course.
Thought I couldn't pull it off?

52:13.048 --> 52:16.468
It's a great engine
with extraordinary power.

52:16.468 --> 52:19.554
It's up to you now, Frisbee.

52:19.554 --> 52:21.806
Right. I'll have this in
the Trans-Am by morning.

52:22.974 --> 52:25.935
With a beefed up stove,
it's good for three loads.

52:29.230 --> 52:30.774
Relax, Pops.

52:30.774 --> 52:34.235
I'm putting my reputation at stake here.

52:39.449 --> 52:43.286
Must be a pre-race party
going on at Roboworld,

52:43.286 --> 52:44.913
The goddess may see those.

52:44.913 --> 52:46.831
Where're you going at this hour?

52:47.082 --> 52:48.291
Gotta go.

52:48.291 --> 52:50.835
Where the hell is he going?

52:51.586 --> 52:54.297
It's the night before the REDLINE.

52:54.297 --> 52:55.423
No idea.

52:59.761 --> 53:01.513
Well, do what you will.

53:12.357 --> 53:15.235
ROBOWORLD UNDERGROUND POWER RELAY STATION

53:15.235 --> 53:16.319
ROBOWORLD UNDERGROUND POWER RELAY STATION

53:16.319 --> 53:17.862
The walls are 800 mm thick cosmo titanium.

53:18.113 --> 53:19.406
Fire the shock-breaker!

53:26.246 --> 53:28.832
They're in! Fucking Robopolice!

53:28.832 --> 53:31.126
Trespassers detected.

53:31.126 --> 53:33.753
Come down from the walk immediately.

53:34.129 --> 53:36.715
You got no business here! Get lost!

53:36.715 --> 53:38.717
Hostile intent detected.

53:40.135 --> 53:41.761
Cease your resistance and surrender.

53:41.970 --> 53:43.555
Shut up!
Over my dead body!

53:46.224 --> 53:48.268
Shoot the Runners till they're down!

53:49.352 --> 53:50.812
You bastard!

53:52.313 --> 53:53.106
Stay the hell down!

54:06.119 --> 54:07.912
What is it?

54:07.912 --> 54:13.293
Disgruntled workers have attacked
our main power station,

54:13.293 --> 54:15.420
so we switched to auxiliary power.

54:15.420 --> 54:20.383
Large-scale weapons are disabled
till the power gets restored.

54:20.383 --> 54:21.259
Damn them!

54:22.135 --> 54:24.262
Rest assured, Mr. President.

54:25.930 --> 54:30.018
We have a secret weapon for those
who enter our atmosphere.

54:30.727 --> 54:35.273
A giant A.l. we've been
developing over the years.

54:35.273 --> 54:39.944
A solar system integrated satellite
weapon unit we call...

54:41.404 --> 54:44.574
...the hyper-disintegreator cannon!

54:44.574 --> 54:45.784
Please take a look.

54:56.377 --> 54:58.254
Hey, Lynchman.

54:58.254 --> 54:59.047
What?

54:59.047 --> 55:02.550
Why did the REDLINE Commission
put us up to this?

55:02.842 --> 55:05.845
If the hyper-disintegrator
blasts everyone to hell,

55:05.845 --> 55:09.057
there won't be any race.
That means no betting.

55:09.057 --> 55:10.558
I see.

55:10.558 --> 55:11.434
Get in.

55:13.603 --> 55:16.397
That won't be good for the fat cats.

55:16.397 --> 55:18.775
You know how much money is riding on this?

55:18.775 --> 55:20.235
No idea.

55:20.235 --> 55:22.570
Enough to buy out a couple of planets.

55:22.570 --> 55:23.571
Oh, wow!

55:23.571 --> 55:27.617
Besides, it's gonna be
great publicity for them.

55:27.617 --> 55:32.539
REDLINE's odds'll go up,
and so will their margins.

55:32.539 --> 55:33.748
I get it.

55:35.500 --> 55:37.669
So this is our target for today?

55:37.669 --> 55:39.671
You got it!

55:46.344 --> 55:50.431
The main power station's system was attacked...

55:50.723 --> 55:54.102
...by pro-REDLINE guerrillas
consisting of low-level workers.

55:59.524 --> 56:01.317
As a result, the RED-RACERS...

56:01.317 --> 56:04.946
are now safe from
heavy ground-based weaponry.

56:04.946 --> 56:08.533
Roboworld officials are currently
working on corrective measures.

56:08.533 --> 56:12.537
According to government sources,
the malfunction of the power system...

56:12.537 --> 56:15.665
...occurred late last night.
When the Robopolice arrived...

56:46.279 --> 56:46.946
What's your name?

56:49.198 --> 56:50.700
JP?

56:50.700 --> 56:51.576
Where did you get that?

56:51.576 --> 56:52.911
Weird name.

56:52.911 --> 56:53.786
I'm Sonoshee.

56:53.786 --> 56:54.621
Sonoshee.

57:17.393 --> 57:20.021
With REDLINE just a day away,

57:20.021 --> 57:25.485
we should keep our eyes on the
racers trying to enter Roboworld.

57:25.485 --> 57:29.781
For this non-stop road race
in the military exercise base,

57:29.781 --> 57:32.492
each driver's course pick will hold the key.

57:33.368 --> 57:37.664
We've been profiling the
REDLINE racers every evening.

57:37.664 --> 57:40.625
On the eve of the big race,
we feature JP,

57:40.625 --> 57:44.629
who's entering only because
another racer dropped out.

57:44.629 --> 57:48.383
Like Lynchman, who's notorious
for his rough play,

57:48.383 --> 57:50.635
JP has a dark past of his own.

57:50.635 --> 57:52.553
According to our research,

57:52.553 --> 57:58.059
this man with a nickname of “Sweet JP“

57:58.059 --> 58:03.439
was indeed a race-fixing
specialist in the past.

58:03.731 --> 58:05.525
What the hell?

58:06.150 --> 58:09.988
This is REDLINE, a festival awaited by
young and old every 5 years.

58:09.988 --> 58:13.908
We need to make sure all concerned
parties are aware of the fact that...

58:15.994 --> 58:18.579
Lucky for me.
It's still running.

58:22.250 --> 58:24.502
REDLINE FINALS DAY

58:32.385 --> 58:34.262
What was that?

58:34.262 --> 58:37.098
I think it's the Supergrass' scout vessel.

58:37.098 --> 58:40.977
The army of that wicked wizard princess, eh?

58:40.977 --> 58:44.063
So, they've teamed up with
the REDLINE now, have they?

58:44.522 --> 58:47.400
Easy does it, easy...

58:47.567 --> 58:49.360
Easy, easy...

58:49.360 --> 58:50.403
Slop!

58:50.778 --> 58:55.074
Too bad you have to race without a test run.

58:55.074 --> 58:56.784
I'll be fine.

58:57.493 --> 58:58.327
JP!

58:58.327 --> 58:59.412
Yeah?

58:59.412 --> 59:00.872
You know the drill, right?

59:01.039 --> 59:03.624
What I know is that it's my show now.

59:18.431 --> 59:20.224
What's that red smoke?

59:39.994 --> 59:40.995
Ta-d ah!

59:41.621 --> 59:43.289
Nice work, Princess.

59:43.498 --> 59:44.082
Piece of cake.

59:44.082 --> 59:45.208
PLANET SUPERGRASS, GRASS HALL
Piece of cake.

59:45.208 --> 59:47.752
PLANET SUPERGRASS, GRASS HALL
Now, all we have to do is to wait for the start.

59:47.752 --> 59:50.129
PLANET SUPERGRASS, GRASS HALL
We're going there to win, alright?

59:50.880 --> 59:56.761
I've just received word
that Supergrass' Red Angels...

59:56.761 --> 59:59.806
have successfully marked the
finish line by the Roboworld Tower.

01:00:01.224 --> 01:00:03.142
That's our princess!

01:00:03.142 --> 01:00:04.727
I guess she made it.

01:00:04.727 --> 01:00:06.145
Of course.

01:00:06.145 --> 01:00:09.398
She's the only one who can use remote magic.

01:00:09.857 --> 01:00:12.235
We must make her proud.

01:00:15.363 --> 01:00:16.531
Morning, Sonoshee!

01:00:17.406 --> 01:00:19.742
Looks like you're mad at me.

01:00:19.742 --> 01:00:22.912
Not really...
We're rivals now anyway.

01:00:22.912 --> 01:00:25.915
Once we're on the race track,
friendship won't count.

01:00:25.915 --> 01:00:27.208
I guess you're right.

01:00:27.208 --> 01:00:28.126
Uh huh.

01:00:32.547 --> 01:00:33.339
Sonoshee.

01:00:33.339 --> 01:00:35.925
Three minutes to drop zone.

01:00:37.343 --> 01:00:38.511
Good luck, then.

01:00:40.847 --> 01:00:42.849
You see the transport ship?

01:00:42.849 --> 01:00:43.599
Yes, Mr. President.

01:00:44.308 --> 01:00:48.104
Let's say the line marked by
our HQ is the finish line.

01:00:48.104 --> 01:00:53.276
At 800 km west above the expected
start line at Knockout Tower,

01:00:53.276 --> 01:00:57.196
we detected an energy reading
from a hyperdimensional drive.

01:00:57.196 --> 01:00:58.990
Hyperdimensional drive?

01:01:00.116 --> 01:01:03.578
How dare they violate our airspace
using a navigation method...

01:01:03.578 --> 01:01:07.123
that's only supposed
to exist in theory!

01:01:07.123 --> 01:01:10.376
I'll teach those RED-RACERS a lesson!

01:01:11.294 --> 01:01:15.131
Titan! Arm the disintegrator cannons!

01:01:15.131 --> 01:01:16.007
Yes, sir!

01:01:34.066 --> 01:01:35.776
Bought your ticket yet?

01:01:35.776 --> 01:01:37.778
Hey! You put it all on Sonoshee.

01:01:37.778 --> 01:01:39.739
Yeah! Sonoshee's my girl.

01:01:39.739 --> 01:01:41.073
You're the man!

01:01:41.073 --> 01:01:42.033
Give me those pork buns!

01:01:42.033 --> 01:01:43.201
Only three left.

01:01:43.201 --> 01:01:44.410
Fine.

01:01:44.410 --> 01:01:45.995
Hey, you! You betting or not?

01:01:45.995 --> 01:01:48.956
Not yet. I'm waiting for the final odds.

01:01:48.956 --> 01:01:49.916
Hot!

01:01:49.916 --> 01:01:53.711
Ew! What a mess!
You're supposed to eat them in one bite.

01:01:53.711 --> 01:01:56.255
Okay guys, last call!

01:01:56.255 --> 01:01:58.049
Anyone who wants to buy in,
step up now.

01:01:58.049 --> 01:02:00.676
One minute to the start!
I'm closing now!

01:02:00.676 --> 01:02:01.802
Give me JP!

01:02:02.011 --> 01:02:04.055
One minute to drop point.

01:02:04.055 --> 01:02:06.599
All racers, please prepare for the drop.

01:02:21.155 --> 01:02:23.407
Deploying apogee motors
on hyper-disintegrator cannons.

01:02:44.679 --> 01:02:48.516
95% energy level.
Stand by on firing button.

01:02:49.892 --> 01:02:52.436
Please put on your light shield, sir.

01:02:53.813 --> 01:02:56.774
Entering drop zone.

01:03:00.319 --> 01:03:03.322
We have an energy reading
on the transport ship.

01:03:03.322 --> 01:03:05.366
It's out of hyperdimensional drive.

01:03:05.366 --> 01:03:07.493
Put it on the monitor.

01:03:09.161 --> 01:03:11.580
Open fire upon visual contact.

01:03:12.164 --> 01:03:13.332
Aye, aye, sir.

01:03:25.845 --> 01:03:27.763
Hyper-disintegrator cannons, fire!

01:03:27.763 --> 01:03:28.681
Firing!

01:03:38.232 --> 01:03:40.651
What's wrong?
Why aren't they firing?

01:03:43.195 --> 01:03:44.405
We have a malfunction.

01:03:44.405 --> 01:03:46.240
What?! That's unacceptable!

01:04:24.528 --> 01:04:27.156
Good morning, all you lucky fans
gathered here today.

01:04:27.156 --> 01:04:29.241
After five years of waiting,
it's the day of the big race!

01:04:29.241 --> 01:04:32.620
We're broadcasting live to the cosmos
for all you crazy fans out there!

01:04:33.204 --> 01:04:35.581
The Red-Machines are being
airdropped to start the race...

01:04:35.581 --> 01:04:38.542
and heading straight toward Knockout Tower.

01:04:38.542 --> 01:04:40.378
If you're looking for a long shot,
here's your man!

01:04:40.378 --> 01:04:42.755
JP with his trademark ducktail.

01:04:42.755 --> 01:04:45.841
His odds are a whopping
25,000 to 1!

01:04:45.841 --> 01:04:48.469
What's going on with that hair?

01:04:48.469 --> 01:04:50.388
But his machine's just as impressive.

01:04:50.388 --> 01:04:51.931
You see every kind of design
imaginable in this race,

01:04:51.931 --> 01:04:55.184
but I don't think anyone's
ever modified a car like JP.

01:04:55.184 --> 01:04:58.938
Looks great. Sweet dedication
from the sweet man.

01:04:58.938 --> 01:05:02.066
Dedication? Maybe.
Or maybe his hair is affecting his brain.

01:05:03.317 --> 01:05:06.779
Calling the race is me,
the rattle-king Void Do.

01:05:06.779 --> 01:05:10.658
And here for commentary is
former RL champ, Mr. Minerva Hanness.

01:05:10.658 --> 01:05:12.159
Stay tuned!

01:05:12.159 --> 01:05:14.078
Damn that REDLINE...

01:05:14.078 --> 01:05:17.623
Mr. President, let my Voltan Corps
take over from here.

01:05:17.623 --> 01:05:19.750
All right.
Show them what you've got!

01:05:20.584 --> 01:05:22.628
Soldiers of the Voltan Corps!

01:05:22.628 --> 01:05:24.004
Our time has come!

01:05:24.547 --> 01:05:27.716
Those racers will be approaching
from three directions.

01:05:27.716 --> 01:05:30.886
Split into three groups to counter them!

01:05:32.847 --> 01:05:34.849
Volton Corps, move out!

01:05:34.849 --> 01:05:35.766
Yes, sir!

01:06:41.999 --> 01:06:44.335
I'm going down! Bye-bye!

01:06:50.966 --> 01:06:53.302
Here comes God Wing followed by Busties!

01:06:53.552 --> 01:06:55.888
Speed Master and Semimaru are right behind.

01:06:56.347 --> 01:06:57.556
Here goes!

01:06:59.433 --> 01:07:02.811
God Wing makes a splash landing,
immediately going for a counterattack!

01:07:04.021 --> 01:07:06.899
What do you do now, Super Boins?

01:07:06.899 --> 01:07:08.400
They're blazing away!

01:07:08.400 --> 01:07:11.654
You can't counterattack unless
you make a swift landing, first!

01:07:12.655 --> 01:07:15.241
Lynchman's gunning for Sonoshee.
Will he catch up?

01:07:15.699 --> 01:07:18.536
Johnny! Shoot a Sidewinder
into Crab Sonoshee.

01:07:18.702 --> 01:07:19.328
Okay!

01:07:34.718 --> 01:07:37.805
Jesus, I'm burning!
That bastard!!

01:07:42.476 --> 01:07:43.352
What the hell?!!

01:07:47.773 --> 01:07:48.607
Huh?

01:07:56.031 --> 01:07:57.116
Fools!

01:08:09.461 --> 01:08:10.754
Ow, hoooottt!!

01:08:13.424 --> 01:08:14.633
YEEEE-HAAAA!

01:08:17.469 --> 01:08:18.262
No way!

01:08:20.139 --> 01:08:21.890
Oh, no!

01:08:22.808 --> 01:08:25.894
Not bad, Colonel Volton.

01:08:26.645 --> 01:08:28.314
Thank you, sir.

01:08:30.316 --> 01:08:31.317
What?

01:08:35.696 --> 01:08:37.573
I see.

01:08:38.574 --> 01:08:42.870
Sir, I just got word we have another problem.

01:08:42.870 --> 01:08:44.371
What now?

01:08:44.371 --> 01:08:48.208
Observe, please.
REDLINE's broadcast ratings.

01:08:48.208 --> 01:08:53.380
82% of the broadcast satellites
in the M3 Nebula...

01:08:53.589 --> 01:08:56.425
are uplinked to that
mothership as a terminal...

01:08:56.425 --> 01:09:00.095
and are beaming live coverage of
the REDLINE to the entire galaxy.

01:09:00.512 --> 01:09:01.972
In other words,

01:09:01.972 --> 01:09:05.017
every secret military asset
and facility on Roboworld...

01:09:05.017 --> 01:09:08.562
Smash those racers
before they reach...

01:09:08.562 --> 01:09:12.066
zone 7X where
Funky Boy is sleeping.

01:09:12.983 --> 01:09:14.735
Funky Boy must not be awakened.

01:09:14.735 --> 01:09:16.945
He's still a baby
barely out of the womb.

01:09:16.945 --> 01:09:20.532
He needs more time
to learn to obey.

01:09:26.747 --> 01:09:27.915
Payback time!

01:09:38.926 --> 01:09:39.885
Suckers!

01:09:51.939 --> 01:09:53.649
Good job, engine three!

01:09:54.817 --> 01:09:56.068
Get a load of this!

01:09:56.068 --> 01:09:59.697
Crab Sonoshee's bravely
charging up the slope!

01:09:59.697 --> 01:10:00.614
Bold move!

01:10:00.614 --> 01:10:03.409
She may be able
to take the short cut,

01:10:03.409 --> 01:10:06.412
but Lynchcar and the Trans-Am
have to go around.

01:10:07.037 --> 01:10:08.539
Johnny! I see the dam!

01:10:08.539 --> 01:10:09.957
Here we go!

01:10:23.303 --> 01:10:24.680
I see you, Lynchman!

01:10:26.473 --> 01:10:30.644
Finally caught up, Cherry Boy Hunter?
I thought you'd retired.

01:10:32.187 --> 01:10:33.147
You wish!

01:10:33.522 --> 01:10:34.523
Don't celebrate yet!

01:10:47.911 --> 01:10:49.538
Yes! Now we're even!

01:10:49.830 --> 01:10:52.541
You're making this interesting,
Sonoshee McLaren!

01:10:55.335 --> 01:10:56.420
Trava...

01:11:02.468 --> 01:11:05.137
Regret leaving me behind in the army?

01:11:06.013 --> 01:11:06.805
Captain Deyzuna!

01:11:06.805 --> 01:11:07.556
What?

01:11:07.556 --> 01:11:09.433
We've spotted a moving target
5 klicks to the west.

01:11:09.433 --> 01:11:12.478
Looks like a RED-RACER.

01:11:12.478 --> 01:11:15.105
Okay, all vehicles,
move onto the target!

01:11:15.314 --> 01:11:16.607
Rogen

01:11:16.607 --> 01:11:19.318
This one's mine.
I'm gonna rip his head off!

01:11:21.111 --> 01:11:24.990
That weasel!
He thinks he can beat me?

01:11:24.990 --> 01:11:29.828
I've been waiting for this
a long time, Trava!

01:11:29.828 --> 01:11:32.581
What do you want, Deyzuna?

01:11:32.581 --> 01:11:35.167
My sand-biker's gonna
whip your sorry ass!

01:11:35.167 --> 01:11:37.628
In your dreams,
you pathetic little shit!

01:11:38.754 --> 01:11:40.005
Come and get me!

01:11:42.966 --> 01:11:45.302
Now let's check out what JP's up to.

01:11:45.302 --> 01:11:48.639
He's finally approaching the dam
way behind the others.

01:11:48.639 --> 01:11:51.350
I think it's time for JP to retire.

01:11:51.350 --> 01:11:52.142
Yeah, really.

01:11:52.142 --> 01:11:56.396
The engine and the machine's
out of balance! Friggin' Frisbee...

01:11:57.105 --> 01:11:59.441
What's wrong, JP?

01:11:59.441 --> 01:12:01.819
Get her up to speed and you're in the clear.

01:12:01.819 --> 01:12:03.487
Don't be afraid to use the gold nitro.

01:12:03.487 --> 01:12:05.989
Never thought I'd need this so soon.

01:12:11.370 --> 01:12:14.164
Whoa, boy! GO!

01:12:20.921 --> 01:12:23.173
He's skipping across!
Do you see that?

01:12:23.173 --> 01:12:24.216
I don't believe it!

01:12:24.216 --> 01:12:25.384
Skipping! Do you see this?!

01:12:25.384 --> 01:12:28.887
You gotta hand it to him.
JP's Trans-Am is impressive.

01:12:28.887 --> 01:12:30.722
He's still way behind the rest, though.

01:12:33.016 --> 01:12:36.562
You're late, Frisbee.

01:12:38.021 --> 01:12:40.816
How's your friend doing so far?

01:12:41.567 --> 01:12:43.861
JP's holding the last place as we planned,

01:12:43.861 --> 01:12:46.572
so his odds will stay low.

01:12:46.572 --> 01:12:49.575
He'll make his move in the last quarter,

01:12:49.575 --> 01:12:51.410
get his odds up, then he loses.

01:12:51.410 --> 01:12:54.288
Same as in the YELLOWLINE.
No problem.

01:12:54.288 --> 01:12:59.585
I'm still worried that
he may wanna win the race.

01:12:59.585 --> 01:13:02.421
That will cost me a great deal, you know.

01:13:02.421 --> 01:13:04.548
There's no guarantee, is there?

01:13:04.548 --> 01:13:06.049
You can relax.

01:13:06.049 --> 01:13:09.553
There won't be any surprises.
I guarantee that.

01:13:09.553 --> 01:13:10.637
Noooooo!

01:13:11.388 --> 01:13:13.432
Stop picking on us!

01:13:18.520 --> 01:13:20.188
Oh, no!

01:13:24.359 --> 01:13:25.819
I've had it!

01:13:25.819 --> 01:13:27.279
Let's roll!

01:13:39.207 --> 01:13:40.375
Hi!

01:13:53.180 --> 01:13:54.556
Coochy-coochy-coo.

01:13:58.352 --> 01:14:00.562
What's going on, Big Deyzuna?!

01:14:00.562 --> 01:14:03.273
Two planes were down before I knew it.

01:14:03.273 --> 01:14:05.859
So you lost a couple of planes.
No big deal!

01:14:05.859 --> 01:14:07.611
Use your head!

01:14:07.611 --> 01:14:08.403
Si"

01:14:08.403 --> 01:14:14.826
Dr. Sabose! Quit playing around
with those pervs and tits!

01:14:14.826 --> 01:14:17.329
Wipe out the racers in
the southern sector already!

01:14:17.329 --> 01:14:18.246
Si"

01:14:18.246 --> 01:14:23.043
Little Deyzuna! Who said you could
leave the unit to be in the REDLINE?

01:14:23.043 --> 01:14:24.878
Sorry, sir! I'll do my best.

01:14:25.587 --> 01:14:29.216
Get back in formation
and corner them to Zone 7X!

01:14:30.384 --> 01:14:32.260
Are you reading me,
Little Deyzuna?

01:14:32.511 --> 01:14:35.180
Colonel Volton, please!

01:14:35.180 --> 01:14:36.306
Don't...

01:14:36.306 --> 01:14:38.725
Don't let this punk make a fool of me.

01:14:40.143 --> 01:14:43.855
Stop raving and get a hold of yourself!

01:14:43.855 --> 01:14:45.899
I repeat once more.

01:14:45.899 --> 01:14:49.069
Get back in formation
and chase them to Zone 7X!

01:14:49.069 --> 01:14:50.779
That's an order from your commander!

01:14:51.029 --> 01:14:53.615
I'm afraid I can't take that order, sir.

01:14:53.615 --> 01:14:55.325
I'm entering the race.

01:14:55.325 --> 01:14:57.285
Have you lost your mind?

01:14:57.285 --> 01:15:00.706
You'll be court-martialed and shot!

01:15:00.706 --> 01:15:05.168
Colonel Voltan...
I know the risk, but I must do this.

01:15:05.168 --> 01:15:06.920
I promise victory!

01:15:06.920 --> 01:15:10.173
No! I can't allow that! Deyz...

01:15:10.173 --> 01:15:13.051
Colonel Volton! Are you going
to just stand by and watch?

01:15:13.510 --> 01:15:15.762
Certainly not, Mr. President!

01:15:17.097 --> 01:15:19.182
Attention, all soldiers of Roboworld!

01:15:19.182 --> 01:15:20.767
All units, scramble!

01:15:20.767 --> 01:15:23.770
Intercept all the RED-RACERs in Zone 7X!

01:15:24.771 --> 01:15:27.858
You said all units, Colonel Voltan?

01:15:27.858 --> 01:15:31.486
You heard me!
Send out all units!

01:15:33.530 --> 01:15:37.409
All racers are converging at
the minefield in Zone 7X.

01:15:37.409 --> 01:15:39.578
God Wing takes the lead
in the northern sector,

01:15:39.578 --> 01:15:40.787
followed by Super Boins.

01:15:40.787 --> 01:15:43.081
From southern sector
comes Crab Sonoshee!

01:15:43.081 --> 01:15:45.876
Trava's Speed Master is
coming from the central sector,

01:15:45.876 --> 01:15:48.837
with Little Deyzuna hot on his tail.

01:15:55.552 --> 01:15:59.097
Speed Master's faster than
the detonators on those mines!

01:15:59.097 --> 01:16:00.807
We just got some new footage.

01:16:00.807 --> 01:16:02.934
Gori Rider's burrowing underground.

01:16:02.934 --> 01:16:06.563
The Miki/Todoroki team
is running right behind him.

01:16:06.563 --> 01:16:10.817
It may be a shortcut,
but speed-wise? I'm not sure.

01:16:10.817 --> 01:16:14.488
Ouch! You think we've cleared 7X by now?

01:16:14.863 --> 01:16:18.241
Probably. Let's get out of here
and take them down!

01:16:18.241 --> 01:16:18.825
All right!

01:16:24.206 --> 01:16:25.499
Let's do it, Miki!

01:16:25.791 --> 01:16:27.209
Go get them, Todoroki!

01:16:27.459 --> 01:16:29.377
GUTS AND GLORY!

01:16:30.003 --> 01:16:30.295
You sure about waking it up?

01:16:30.295 --> 01:16:32.839
XXXXXXXpoint (BASE 7x) - UNDERGROUND
You sure about waking it up?

01:16:32.839 --> 01:16:34.382
XXXXXXXpoint (BASE 7X) - UNDERGROUND

01:16:34.382 --> 01:16:37.427
Yeah. The bioweapon asleep
in Roboworld's untouchable area,

01:16:37.427 --> 01:16:38.845
a.k.a. "Funky Boy."

01:16:38.845 --> 01:16:42.724
We have to count on him
to fight Volton's troops.

01:16:43.475 --> 01:16:48.688
Guts and glory! Guts and glory!

01:16:51.066 --> 01:16:52.234
We're coming out!

01:16:54.111 --> 01:16:55.487
Guts and glory!

01:16:55.487 --> 01:16:58.615
There! Miki and Todoroki are making their move!

01:16:58.615 --> 01:17:00.617
They've taken the lead!

01:17:00.867 --> 01:17:03.411
Yes, Miki! We're in the lead!

01:17:04.079 --> 01:17:04.746
Mine!

01:17:10.752 --> 01:17:15.090
Looks like JP's made it to Zone 7X somehow.

01:17:15.090 --> 01:17:17.592
What do you mean "somehow"?

01:17:21.888 --> 01:17:23.348
Frisbee.

01:17:24.307 --> 01:17:26.643
You do know this is business?

01:17:27.435 --> 01:17:29.354
Of course I do.

01:17:36.444 --> 01:17:37.195
Huh?!

01:17:41.491 --> 01:17:43.869
Look, flying carriers!

01:17:43.869 --> 01:17:46.454
I see they've decided to
send in Air-Destroyers.

01:17:46.454 --> 01:17:47.205
Uh-oh!

01:17:47.956 --> 01:17:49.875
Colonel Volton's getting serious.

01:18:07.726 --> 01:18:09.144
He kicked me!

01:18:13.940 --> 01:18:15.150
There's no end to them!

01:18:15.150 --> 01:18:17.444
Ouch, ouch!

01:18:17.444 --> 01:18:18.653
Lynchman!

01:18:18.653 --> 01:18:20.447
Johnny, come closer!

01:18:20.447 --> 01:18:21.239
Okay!

01:18:22.908 --> 01:18:24.826
Todoroki!
Time to use the thunderbolt!

01:18:24.826 --> 01:18:26.036
Rotate 120 degrees!

01:18:26.286 --> 01:18:27.537
Guts and glory!

01:18:32.751 --> 01:18:33.752
Shit, I missed!

01:18:35.629 --> 01:18:37.255
We did it!

01:18:40.717 --> 01:18:41.593
Launch flares!

01:18:50.018 --> 01:18:52.270
That should teach them a lesson.

01:18:52.270 --> 01:18:55.273
Those racers are as good as dead.

01:18:55.273 --> 01:18:57.859
There's no need for any further attack.

01:18:58.568 --> 01:19:01.988
Mr. President.
Did you think I'd stop now?

01:19:01.988 --> 01:19:04.866
You can't afford to
take pity on that scum.

01:19:05.951 --> 01:19:07.118
All right, then.

01:19:30.350 --> 01:19:32.143
Damn, I can't break it!

01:19:32.143 --> 01:19:34.104
Yes, you can!
Smash it with your rage!

01:19:37.482 --> 01:19:40.235
What is this place?!

01:20:06.261 --> 01:20:08.805
I'm coming to get you, Sonoshee.

01:20:22.986 --> 01:20:26.114
What the...?!
That's a bioweapon!

01:20:26.114 --> 01:20:28.908
Isn't that against the
peace treaty, Mr. Minerva?

01:20:28.908 --> 01:20:32.329
I have a feeling we're not
supposed to be seeing this.

01:20:49.512 --> 01:20:50.805
How can Funky Boy be...?!

01:20:50.805 --> 01:20:52.182
I don't believe this!

01:20:52.182 --> 01:20:57.187
Mr. President, Funky Boy
will destroy Roboworld.

01:20:57.437 --> 01:21:00.732
Besides that, that giant bioweapon
is a clear violation of...

01:21:00.732 --> 01:21:04.694
the M3 Nebula Peace Treaty,
and there are no scapegoats to pin this on!

01:21:04.694 --> 01:21:07.614
We must take measures immediately!

01:21:07.614 --> 01:21:09.991
You must make a decision, sir!

01:21:11.409 --> 01:21:12.660
Mr. President!

01:21:13.787 --> 01:21:17.624
Mr. President, we have the
hyper-disintegrator cannons back on line.

01:21:17.624 --> 01:21:20.502
They'll be ready to fire
as soon as charging completes.

01:21:25.590 --> 01:21:28.468
Agghhh...Hail the President!

01:21:29.928 --> 01:21:32.514
Target Funky Boy!
He's out of control!

01:21:32.889 --> 01:21:33.890
Yes, sir.

01:21:39.521 --> 01:21:43.900
Target's set.
We can fire at any time.

01:21:44.567 --> 01:21:47.821
All right.
Take him down in one shot!

01:21:47.821 --> 01:21:49.823
Yes, sir.
Give me the command.

01:21:55.578 --> 01:21:57.622
Fire the hyper-disintegrator cannons!

01:21:57.622 --> 01:21:58.248
Firing!

01:22:25.859 --> 01:22:27.485
Princess!

01:22:30.196 --> 01:22:32.866
Excellent!
We wiped them out clean.

01:22:33.199 --> 01:22:35.535
Energy discharge, complete.

01:22:35.702 --> 01:22:37.120
Now recharging.

01:22:38.455 --> 01:22:40.582
This can't be happening.

01:22:40.582 --> 01:22:41.624
Are they really dead?

01:22:42.292 --> 01:22:43.418
I don't believe this.

01:22:43.793 --> 01:22:46.212
They actually used
hyper-disintegrator cannons.

01:22:47.213 --> 01:22:48.923
It looks like everyone's
been wiped out.

01:22:50.925 --> 01:22:52.969
That bastard planted something!

01:23:00.477 --> 01:23:02.979
Sonoshee, you alright?

01:23:02.979 --> 01:23:03.897
JP.

01:23:05.273 --> 01:23:07.525
You okay, Captain Sabose?

01:23:07.525 --> 01:23:08.693
I'm okay.

01:23:08.693 --> 01:23:10.945
How many planes are left?

01:23:10.945 --> 01:23:13.031
18, including the ones that got damaged.

01:23:13.031 --> 01:23:15.158
16 sand-bikers left in another unit.

01:23:15.158 --> 01:23:17.702
The crossjet unit's been wiped out

01:23:17.702 --> 01:23:21.539
I see... The RED-RACERS
are in equally bad shape.

01:23:21.539 --> 01:23:23.374
Wait for Colonel Volton's orders.

01:23:23.374 --> 01:23:24.167
Roger.

01:23:47.899 --> 01:23:53.112
C'mon, Sonoshee. Winning the
REDLINE's your dream, right?

01:23:54.405 --> 01:23:56.491
I'm only halfway there.

01:23:57.784 --> 01:24:00.370
I didn't get to see the finish line.

01:24:00.370 --> 01:24:05.208
I'll show you. Not much room,
but you don't mind, do you?

01:24:05.208 --> 01:24:08.795
The machine's gonna be too heavy.
You can't win.

01:24:09.504 --> 01:24:10.838
Yes, I will.

01:24:11.172 --> 01:24:14.551
We'll win this together!

01:24:22.559 --> 01:24:27.313
That's sweet, JP,
but I have to ask you something.

01:24:28.773 --> 01:24:32.110
Kinda busy right now!

01:24:32.360 --> 01:24:35.238
No. I need to ask you now.

01:24:37.115 --> 01:24:37.991
Fine!

01:24:38.157 --> 01:24:42.996
Have you been arrested
for fixing a race?

01:24:49.586 --> 01:24:50.587
Yeah.

01:24:50.587 --> 01:24:51.588
What happened?

01:24:54.591 --> 01:24:57.343
It was a Yellow MAX series 8 years ago.

01:24:58.094 --> 01:25:01.222
Our team was on a hot winning streak.

01:25:02.056 --> 01:25:06.102
Frisbee decided to hook up
with the mafia,

01:25:06.102 --> 01:25:09.230
so he could get a
better engine and parts.

01:25:10.690 --> 01:25:15.028
I entered the race
with his life on the line...

01:25:15.028 --> 01:25:16.529
...and I lost.

01:25:16.529 --> 01:25:20.283
After that, he desperately needed the money.

01:25:21.326 --> 01:25:23.870
But there's a sting operation
against the lnuki gang.

01:25:23.870 --> 01:25:27.332
They found stuff pointing to Frisbee.
He was trapped.

01:25:27.332 --> 01:25:30.376
That friggin' Frisbee's gonna get JP killed!

01:25:30.376 --> 01:25:33.588
So you went to prison for him.

01:25:33.588 --> 01:25:37.925
He believed in me and
risked his life so I could race.

01:25:37.925 --> 01:25:40.762
I always owe him for that.

01:25:42.930 --> 01:25:47.060
Then we'll just have to pay him back
by winning the REDLINE.

01:25:51.189 --> 01:25:52.690
You're gonna help me?

01:25:56.110 --> 01:25:59.530
If you help me make
my dream come true.

01:26:00.198 --> 01:26:01.115
Of course.

01:26:16.964 --> 01:26:19.175
This is his regeneration function.

01:26:19.175 --> 01:26:21.678
There must have been
some pieces of him left.

01:26:21.678 --> 01:26:22.804
Secretary Titan!

01:26:22.804 --> 01:26:26.557
Finish him off with the hyper-disintegrator cannons!

01:26:26.557 --> 01:26:30.103
Negative. We need another
two hours to recharge it.

01:26:31.562 --> 01:26:33.690
Where's Volton now?

01:26:33.690 --> 01:26:38.319
I never thought I'd see this day.
Is it ready?

01:26:38.319 --> 01:26:39.404
Yes, it's ready!

01:26:39.404 --> 01:26:41.072
Can we control it?

01:26:41.072 --> 01:26:45.243
With your skill, no problem.

01:26:45.243 --> 01:26:48.913
You just like the idea of
getting new data, don't you?

01:26:48.913 --> 01:26:50.873
Very well. Proceed.

01:26:58.423 --> 01:27:01.551
Oh, no...Princeeeess!

01:27:11.352 --> 01:27:15.273
This feels great! Wonderful!

01:27:15.273 --> 01:27:17.358
I can feel the power!

01:27:29.871 --> 01:27:31.706
Let's get out of here, Shinkai!

01:27:31.706 --> 01:27:32.123
Okay!
Let's get out of here, Shinkai!

01:27:37.962 --> 01:27:40.548
All right! Gori-police custom rider!

01:27:51.517 --> 01:27:55.396
You morons! The RED-RACERS
are running again.

01:27:55.730 --> 01:27:57.899
Go after them, now!

01:27:57.899 --> 01:27:58.900
Yes, sir!

01:27:58.900 --> 01:28:00.318
We should get going.

01:28:02.653 --> 01:28:04.197
This is the machine
your friend tuned up?

01:28:04.197 --> 01:28:04.989
Yeah.

01:28:05.948 --> 01:28:06.866
You ready?

01:28:06.866 --> 01:28:07.408
Yeah.

01:28:17.668 --> 01:28:20.963
Frisbee! With the beefed up stove you gave me,

01:28:20.963 --> 01:28:22.965
Sonoshee and I will blast to the top!

01:28:41.776 --> 01:28:43.986
Your friend has done well.

01:28:45.196 --> 01:28:46.155
Yes.

01:28:46.155 --> 01:28:47.949
It's time we wrapped this up.

01:28:47.949 --> 01:28:50.993
We're in third.
The odds are looking up.

01:28:51.828 --> 01:28:53.579
That should give us enough.

01:28:53.579 --> 01:28:56.916
No point in getting greedy
and ending up in the hole, Frisbee.

01:28:56.916 --> 01:28:59.293
Time to detonate the bomb.

01:28:59.919 --> 01:29:02.672
Wait till JP grabs the lead, please.

01:29:02.672 --> 01:29:04.674
You promised me!

01:29:05.633 --> 01:29:07.176
Then here's a check!

01:29:07.176 --> 01:29:11.556
Double what you got for
the YELLOWLINE race. Take it!

01:29:13.391 --> 01:29:15.142
We're running out of time.

01:29:15.142 --> 01:29:19.480
I'm paying both you and JP enough money.

01:29:19.480 --> 01:29:23.776
What're you complaining about?
Gimme the detonator!

01:29:23.985 --> 01:29:28.906
I want to see this race to the end.
To see us- No...

01:29:29.115 --> 01:29:31.492
I want to see him win!

01:29:37.665 --> 01:29:39.041
Sorry, Frisbee.

01:29:39.041 --> 01:29:42.336
Nothing personal.
It's just business.

01:29:44.839 --> 01:29:47.550
I don't wanna hurt you.
Just hand me the damn thing.

01:29:49.635 --> 01:29:52.138
Over my dead body!

01:29:53.014 --> 01:29:54.932
Suit yourself. You're dead!

01:30:00.855 --> 01:30:01.856
BYE-bye!

01:30:11.240 --> 01:30:13.034
Pops... Why are you here?

01:30:15.286 --> 01:30:17.496
I'll keep this with me for now.
Got that?!

01:30:19.123 --> 01:30:21.500
I didn't come here
to save you!

01:30:21.500 --> 01:30:25.713
But a team mechanic's
gotta see the race through.

01:30:25.713 --> 01:30:27.798
The driver, the mechanic,
and the junk dealer...

01:30:27.798 --> 01:30:31.469
Those three make a team, right?

01:30:34.055 --> 01:30:37.475
God Wing in the lead
is struggling to take control.

01:30:37.475 --> 01:30:40.269
He sustained quite a bit
of damage this time around.

01:30:40.269 --> 01:30:42.271
Hey! Clear the way!

01:30:45.191 --> 01:30:48.069
Machine Head!
Quit tearing up the road!

01:30:50.988 --> 01:30:53.199
I'm having a ball!

01:30:54.158 --> 01:30:55.368
The outside course is clear!

01:30:55.368 --> 01:30:57.411
We can't get there at this speed.

01:30:57.411 --> 01:30:57.995
There!

01:31:00.581 --> 01:31:02.208
Go for it!

01:31:06.712 --> 01:31:07.296
You're here.

01:31:08.214 --> 01:31:09.799
Finally caught up with you.

01:31:09.799 --> 01:31:14.595
You got the guts to use
the steamlight, Sonoshee?

01:31:14.804 --> 01:31:17.598
Huh? That's the same as yours...

01:31:17.807 --> 01:31:19.642
As a courtesy to
stubborn racers like you,

01:31:19.642 --> 01:31:22.103
I won't beat you just yet!

01:31:22.103 --> 01:31:23.396
Bring it on!

01:31:24.897 --> 01:31:28.609
Behold!
The platinum nitro charge!

01:31:36.826 --> 01:31:40.538
And there it is!
Machine Head's Platinum nitro charge!!

01:31:40.913 --> 01:31:43.416
The only man to master the steamlight.

01:31:43.416 --> 01:31:45.543
Looks like the king's gonna win again!

01:31:50.798 --> 01:31:52.299
Hey, Sonoshee!

01:31:52.299 --> 01:31:54.927
We made a deal.
Make my dream come true!

01:32:00.141 --> 01:32:00.850
Second spot is mine!

01:32:05.396 --> 01:32:07.815
Think you can get me?!

01:32:21.746 --> 01:32:24.081
That fool!
He's using steamlight?!

01:32:24.081 --> 01:32:25.624
No man can handle that!

01:32:25.624 --> 01:32:27.334
You can do it, JP!

01:32:27.334 --> 01:32:28.836
Seriously?

01:32:30.087 --> 01:32:30.838
Search me.

01:32:32.923 --> 01:32:34.967
Ow... Hooott!!

01:32:34.967 --> 01:32:38.220
Trying to be funny, huh?
Let's see what he's got.

01:32:39.430 --> 01:32:41.515
Let's roll, Todoroki!

01:32:41.515 --> 01:32:42.349
Guts and glory!

01:32:45.686 --> 01:32:47.438
Sorry, Deyzuna. Time's up.

01:32:48.355 --> 01:32:49.732
Let's go, Shinkai!

01:32:49.732 --> 01:32:50.858
Here we come!

01:32:51.776 --> 01:32:53.110
Don't leave me!

01:33:07.666 --> 01:33:08.542
No way.

01:33:09.418 --> 01:33:11.295
We'll never catch up with them.

01:33:11.295 --> 01:33:12.421
Hold on a minute, Mr. Minerva!

01:33:12.421 --> 01:33:13.214
Huh?

01:33:13.214 --> 01:33:16.926
The finish line's on top
of the Dest Tower, isn't it?

01:33:16.926 --> 01:33:21.138
No one can climb up the wall to reach the line!

01:33:21.138 --> 01:33:21.722
What'll they do?

01:33:22.389 --> 01:33:23.766
Princess, what's...?

01:33:23.766 --> 01:33:25.226
Watch and see.

01:33:33.734 --> 01:33:35.027
What the...?!

01:33:35.027 --> 01:33:36.237
Check this out!

01:33:36.237 --> 01:33:39.740
The REDLINE mothership has warped out
beneath the Dest Tower...

01:33:39.907 --> 01:33:41.742
and became the final straightway!

01:33:43.035 --> 01:33:44.245
You see it now?

01:33:44.620 --> 01:33:48.749
The final straightway has
been joined to the finish line!

01:33:52.044 --> 01:33:53.963
Ugh... Sonoshee...

01:33:55.005 --> 01:33:56.173
Let's do it!

01:34:04.056 --> 01:34:07.059
JP's moving up like a bullet!
What's going on?

01:34:07.059 --> 01:34:09.812
Unbelievable!
This is unbelievable!

01:34:11.188 --> 01:34:14.275
I'm gonna win.

01:34:14.275 --> 01:34:17.987
I'm the king of kings!
You know what that means, JP?

01:34:17.987 --> 01:34:21.157
It means victory belongs to me!

01:34:21.157 --> 01:34:25.536
I'm gonna win.
I've got a goddess at my side!

01:34:32.501 --> 01:34:36.714
Here they come!
Here come JP and Sonoshee!

01:34:57.401 --> 01:34:58.485
I see it!

01:35:08.454 --> 01:35:13.542
JP! You need an edge
to win the REDLINE!

01:35:13.542 --> 01:35:16.337
You don't deserve to win this race!

01:35:19.006 --> 01:35:23.302
Goddamn it! I need something
to juice this thing up...!

01:35:23.302 --> 01:35:25.846
Frisbee! ls there anything?!

01:35:25.846 --> 01:35:27.681
There's nothing left!

01:35:35.606 --> 01:35:38.901
Whoa! JP's engine has blown!
It's blown!

01:35:39.276 --> 01:35:41.570
But wait...
He's picking up speed somehow.

01:36:11.558 --> 01:36:13.686
Victory's mine, JP!

01:36:17.648 --> 01:36:18.732
JP!

01:36:18.899 --> 01:36:19.775
Sonoshee!

01:36:57.354 --> 01:36:59.815
It's JP and Sonoshee!
They're the winners!

01:37:00.107 --> 01:37:06.113
JP and Sonoshee! JP and Sonoshee
came in top at the finish line!

01:37:06.113 --> 01:37:08.115
JP! JP!

01:37:08.115 --> 01:37:10.034
Sonoshee! Sonoshee!

01:37:10.367 --> 01:37:12.161
He's done it!

01:37:21.378 --> 01:37:23.630
Interesting...

01:37:32.473 --> 01:37:34.516
Oh... That's beautiful.

01:37:38.812 --> 01:37:40.022
Sonoshee.

01:37:41.357 --> 01:37:43.108
I love you.

01:37:43.609 --> 01:37:46.195
I love you, too, JP.
